      "The idea is not new. France is often credited with pioneering it: a law passed in 2016 requires larger companies to negotiate with unions on how employees can switch off. Several other European countries, including Spain, Belgium and Portugal, have adopted their own versions. The details vary widely, but they all reflect the same concern: when work can follow people everywhere, the boundary between professional and private life starts to disappear.",
